    "references": [
      {
        "line": 47,
        "text": "let rng,S,seq=0,queue=[],history=[],disposed=false,tacticsController=null;"
      },
      {
        "line": 62,
        "text": "rng=mulberry32(newSeed>>>0);seq=0;queue=[];history=[];"
      },
      {
        "line": 1180,
        "text": "replay(seconds=C.replay.seconds){const n=Math.round(seconds*C.replay.hz);return history.slice(-n);},"
      },
      {
        "line": 1193,
        "text": "dispose(){disposed=true;queue=[];history=[];},"
      },
      {
        "line": 1195,
        "text": "function recordHistory(){if(S.tick%Math.round(60/C.replay.hz))return;history.push(engine.snapshot());const max=C.replay.seconds*C.replay.hz*2;if(history.length>max)history.splice(0,history.length-max);}"
      }
    ],
    "observations": [
      "Every recordHistory invocation follows S.tick++, so tick is a positive finite integer.",
      "hz=0 makes Math.round(60/hz)=Infinity; tick%Infinity=tick is truthy, returning before snapshot allocation.",
      "history is used only by reset, recordHistory, replay getter and disposal; physics and AI never read it.",
      "snapshot/snapshotPlayers/speedCap/eff only read state and allocate derived values; they neither draw RNG nor advance clocks.",
      "The bot adapter never calls engine.replay. Replay presentation is already excluded from the headless measurement."
    ]
  },
